,title,link,text,language,family
0,Kutchi-Swahili - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kutchi-Swahili,"Kutchi-Swahili, or Cutchi-Swahili, is a Swahili-based creole derived from the Kutchi language of the Kutch district in the Indian state of Gujarat and spoken among the Indian population of East Africa.",Cutchi-Swahili,Creole
1,Kutchi-Swahili,https://grokipedia.com/page/kutchi_swahili,"Kutchi-Swahili, also known as Cutchi-Swahili, is an endangered Swahili-based creole language primarily spoken by the Kutchi ethnic community in East Africa, particularly in Tanzania and Kenya.",Cutchi-Swahili,Creole
2,Cutchi-Swahili Language (CCL)... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/ccl/,"Cutchi-Swahili is an endangered indigenous language of Tanzania. It is a Swahili-based creole. The language is used as a first language by all adults in the ethnic community, but not all young people. It is not known to be taught in schools.",Cutchi-Swahili,Creole
3,Creole Languages,https://www.tomedes.com/translator-hub/creole-languages,"A Swahili-based creole, Cutchi-Swahili is spoken by approximately 46,000 people in Kenya and Tanzania. Malay Kupang.",Cutchi-Swahili,Creole
4,Creole Languages | About World Languages,https://www.mustgo.com/worldlanguages/creole-languages/,"Such languages are called creoles. The difference between pidgins and creoles is that people grow up speaking creoles as their first language, whereas nobody speaks pidgin as their first language. There is no single accepted theory that explains the genesis of creole languages.",Cutchi-Swahili,Creole
